Last year I had a problem where emails marked as "Spam" in Gmail were not being forwarded to my main inbox.<p>Someone had the same problem and submitted it to Hacker News:<p>http://iamnotaprogrammer.com/Dont-Forward-Google-Apps-to-Gmail.html<p>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4621571<p>In that topic, rather than use Forwarding, someone suggested a negative Filter. If an email does not contain a random set of charters, filter it out and forward it.<p>I've been using, also suggested in that topic:<p><pre><code>    -{"X5O!P%@AP[4\PZX54(P^)7CC)7}$EICAR-STANDARD-ANTIVIRUS-TEST-FILE!$H+H*"}
</code></pre>
